WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:02.480
<i>Carnage!</i>

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.190
<i>In Hindu mythology,</i>

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.310
<i>it indicates the location of the battle
of Asura demigods and the King of Heaven,</i>

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.480
<i>but at present, it's mainly used
to mean two other things.</i>

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.490
<i>The first is crunch time
right before a deadline.</i>

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.240
<i>And the other...</i>

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.500
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.000
<i>is a scene of difficulties
between two people!</i>

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.260
Please eat it.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:59.050
Give me a break. You eat it, Shinomiya.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.510
KAGUYA WON'T FORGIVE

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:03.760
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.390
<i>If I hadn't eaten any...</i>

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.480
<i>Explaining this situation requires
two incidents to be touched on.</i>

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.900
THE FIRST INCIDENT:
"THE KAGUYA HOME VISIT INCIDENT"

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.780
<i>Kaguya was out of it with a fever
when she pulled Shirogane into her bed.</i>

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:24.160
SCOOP: KAGUYA HOME
VISIT INCIDENT
THE CARETAKER
WAS WATCHING!!

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.410
<i>As a result, they slept next to each other
for hours and nothing more,</i>

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.990
<i>but when Kaguya came to her senses,</i>

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.370
<i>she was justifiably bewildered
and flew into a rage.</i>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.920
<i>However, an on-the-scene inspection
proved Shirogane innocent for the time being,</i>

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.460
<i>and they handled it like adults.</i>

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.040
<i>I apologize for yelling at you.</i>

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.380
<i>No, it's my fault.</i>

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.420
<i>They reconciled, but...</i>

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.430
<i>there was still ill will!</i>

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.840
<i>In Kaguya's point of view,</i>

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.930
<i>he took advantage of her when she was
weakened with a cold, sharing her bed.</i>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.680
<i>Maybe he touched her
when she was sleeping?</i>

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.440
<i>It made her feel uneasy.</i>

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.230
<i>And if he didn't do anything,</i>

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.310
<i>that ticked her off, too!</i>

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.820
<i>It made her feel dissatisfied.</i>

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:58.570
<i>But as for Shirogane,
he had a bone to pick, too.</i>

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.950
<i>He was the one
dragged into Shinomiya's bed,</i>

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.280
<i>and not only did she not understand
a man's hardship</i>

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.870
<i>of exerting every iota of self-restraint,
barely holding on,</i>

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.200
<i>but she also continued
to view him with suspicion.</i>

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.210
<i>So, it was only natural that he harbor
some resentment toward her.</i>

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.800
<i>These feelings of discontent would continue
to mount, leading to an inevitable blowup.</i>

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.960
THE SECOND INCIDENT:
"THE CAKE INCIDENT"!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.720
EARLIER

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.720
What's this?

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.010
It's from the headmaster.
Help yourself.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.220
Yay!

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.730
This is all the cake there is?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.940
I wish the headmaster
were more considerate.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.770
He should've at least given us
enough for all the members.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:39.490
Well, earlier, you and I
were the only ones here, President, so...

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.070
Don't worry. Eat up, Ishigami.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.030
I don't need any.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.870
No, please have it, President.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.700
Don't mind me.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.540
It's okay. You eat it, Shinomiya.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.120
No, no, you, President.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.670
No, really, go ahead.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:53.540
No, I insist.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.420
I insist!

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.710
No, I insist!

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.630
Just eat it already!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.930
You should eat it, President!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.760
<i>Discontent. This is where it blows up!</i>

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:13.270
ONE MINUTE LATER

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.970
Girls like this kind of thing,
so don't hold back.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.270
You don't have an aversion to sweets,
do you, President? So, please.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.270
<i>Essentially polite,
willing to give up their share.</i>

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.270
Look, while you're arguing,
it's getting mushy.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:20.650
FIVE MINUTES LATER

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.110
<i>But as the minutes passed,
it entered into a new phase.</i>

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.360
Yes, right.
And it's almost time to go home.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.650
I'm a slow eater,
so by all means, President.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.150
My hand's already getting tired
from holding this plate!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.150
20 MINUTES LATER

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.280
If you eat it, this whole issue
would be settled peacefully, right?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.910
You're so stubborn.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.910
ONE HOUR LATER

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.660
Would you just eat it, already?

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.540
There's no need for you
to be so obstinate here, President.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.340
<i>After an hour of this, no one would object
to it being called "a scene of carnage."</i>

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.050
<i>The place had turned into
an underworld of mingled resentment!</i>

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.630
The cake wants you
to eat it, too, President!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.300
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.260
<i>If I hadn't eaten a piece,
this never would've happened.</i>

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.800
Use common sense when you speak!
Cake can't talk!

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.560
Prove to me that cake can't talk!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.180
<i>This has become a disaster.</i>

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.810
Extraordinary claims
require extraordinary proof!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.810
<i>I've got it!</i>

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.390
<i>Fujiwara-senpai!</i>

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.360
<i>Fujiwara-senpai is the only one
who can stop those two!</i>

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.490
Why are you being so pigheaded
about not eating it?

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.400
There's a limit
to how stubborn one can be!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.240
Yes, I admit to being stubborn!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.780
But it's because of something
you said before, Shinomiya!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.540
Just what did I say?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.210
It was right after we both started
in the student council!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.500
<i>Do you have any hobbies, Shinomiya?</i>

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.920
<i>No, but is that any of your business?</i>

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.760
<i>Not really.</i>

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.850
<i>It's just that your eyes are so lifeless.</i>

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.520
<i>I was wondering
if there was anything that you liked.</i>

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.100
<i>Something I like...</i>

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.520
<i>Shortcake.</i>

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.270
That's what you said!

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.530
I could never forget that face!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.660
Why would you remember
something so trivial from that long ago?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.160
How could I forget?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.160
Is that right? Is that right?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.540
The tip of my nose itches!
I'm going to scratch!

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.040
Don't mind me!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.920
Sure, scratch all you like!

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.300
<i>He remembered from that long ago.</i>

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.850
If that's your story,
then I've got one, too!

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.510
What?

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.220
The end of last year!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.890
<i>What are you going to do
for Christmas, President?</i>

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.190
<i>Work.</i>

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.690
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.360
<i>That's tough.</i>

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.650
<i>Not especially.</i>

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.610
<i>To me, Christmas is just another day.</i>

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:35.200
<i>My old man gives me a gift certificate
for 2,000 yen worth of books. That's it.</i>

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.170
<i>We don't really celebrate,
and I've never had Christmas cake.</i>

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.460
<i>Not that I'm envious or anything.</i>

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:46.550
Hearing that made me kind of sad!

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.930
You've never been able to have it before,
so I want you to eat this cake, President!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.640
You remember that?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.270
Is that right? Is that right?

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.730
Actually, my forehead itches!
Never mind me while I scratch it!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.730
Scratch away! I don't care!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.240
Enough!

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.990
Since it's come to this, I have an idea!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.490
For today only, I'll feed you!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.500
No, just the opposite!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.410
I'll feed you, Shinomiya!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.500
Please don't steal my feeding idea!

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.000
Don't be shy! Just open your mouth!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.750
You open your mouth, Shinomiya!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:31.880
- Open wide!
- Open wide!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:37.140
This isn't getting us anywhere!
You have a bite, and then I'll have a bite!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.520
No, you go first! If you eat it, I'll eat it!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.350
No complaints if we eat
at the same time?

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.400
That's fine!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.150
GRR GRR

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.150
Here I go!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.040
This is the Friend Police!

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.210
Are you the naughty kids
who've been fighting?

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:11.420
NO FIGHTING!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.420
IF YOU CAN'T GET ALONG,
I'LL CONFISCATE YOUR CAKE!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.180
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:18.930
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.930
<i>Kaguya and Shirogane lose.</i>

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.930
KAGUYA AND SHIROGANE LOSE

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:22.940
WAR CRIMINAL

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.940
MMM, YUMMY

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.190
Romantic advice?

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:30.530
Well, it's not really romantic, but...

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:32.280
KAGUYA WANTS TO FORGIVE

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.570
advice about the opposite sex.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:36.820
Um, like a good way to make up with someone
of the opposite sex you had a fight with.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.540
Since you have a boyfriend,
Miss Kashiwagi,

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.960
I thought maybe you'd have
some useful advice.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.170
Seriously?

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.300
You're asking me for romantic advice?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.050
Well, not exactly romantic,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.600
I want to see if you know a way

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.560
to make peace with someone
of the opposite sex you had a fight with.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.810
I see. In that case,
you've come to the right person.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.110
I'm the Love Master.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.190
Seriously?

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.650
I'm kidding.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.940
You're kidding?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.070
But I do read a lot of romcom manga.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.200
I guess that would work.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.370
I'm asking for a friend.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.830
When you put it like that,

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.420
it sounds like you're talking
about yourself, President.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.340
But you wouldn't be that clichéd,
would you?

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:30.960
Yeah, right, as if.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.590
So...

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:38.590
So, Miss Shinomiya, what were you
and this person fighting about?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.350
Well...

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:43.350
By the way, I'm asking for a friend.
It's not me.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.850
<i>This is definitely about Miss Shinomiya.</i>

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.650
A friend of mine, a girl,
came down with a cold,

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.610
and then, a boy visited her at home.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:57.200
But while she was delirious
with a fever...

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.610
Um...

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.740
I guess you could say they slept together.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.790
When she woke up,
the boy was in bed next to her.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:09.290
That's terrible! Shameless!
What a brute!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.130
Of course...

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.880
nothing happened!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:18.380
In fact, the girl was so out of it
that it's possible she initiated...

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:19.970
Even so!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.050
It's especially when a girl
is in a weakened state

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.140
that the man must have morals
and not do anything!

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:28.520
I agree. That's the correct way
to see it, right?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.190
That boy doesn't have any morals, right?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.770
Right? Right? Right? Right?
Right? Right? Right? Right?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.770
RIGHT!?

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.030
What's wrong with that girl?

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.200
She sounds like a lunatic!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.160
What kind of woman invites you into her bed,
then berates you the next morning?

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.240
Sounds like she's got no morals.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.040
That woman sounds like
a real pain in the ass.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.170
In a romcom, she'd be the standard
black-haired, flat-chested type.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.210
Typical, typical.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.170
<i>Incredible. Once he gets going,
he doesn't stop.</i>

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.050
Being loopy with a fever is no excuse.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.180
I mean, she pulled a dude into bed.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.840
Bet you anything she's a nympho.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.180
At a glance, she's prim and proper,
not to mention stuck-up.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.470
The way she expresses
her sexual desire is twisted, selfish!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.100
She says, "I'm not interested in men,"
but with a handsome guy,

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.690
she'll get her teeth into him
in no time!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.190
If a man is a wolf,
then, a woman's a snake.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.820
Quick to get entangled
and swallows the tail.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.740
Ouroboros, I'm telling you!
Not me! Not this cat!

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:20.570
I'm sure after the guy left, she rubbed—

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.280
Okay, hit the brakes, Ishigami.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.790
Look, even so, the guy really
shouldn't have gone along with it.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:32.460
There had to be a gentle way
of getting out of it, but he just didn't do it.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.590
No.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.960
He probably didn't want to get out of it.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.720
- Fight!
- Yeah!

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:44.720
But they apologized to each other
about it, so it's settled.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:52.230
The thing is, after that, the boy acted
totally normal as if nothing had happened.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:54.230
I feel you.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:59.610
The girl is like on pins and needles,
while the guy has already moved on...

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.990
when it wasn't just some minor mishap.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.490
Exactly!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:10.120
So, it's only natural for her
to be a little annoyed with him, right?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.120
Of course!

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.960
In the first place,
they were in the same bed,

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.630
so the man should take responsibility
and tell her how he feels about her!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.170
Th-That's right!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.010
He's being too irresponsible, right?

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.720
Right? Right? Right?

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.970
Shut up, you moron!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.140
They apologized to each other, right?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.180
Then, it should be over and done with!

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.560
Why the hell is she dragging it out?

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.980
<i>He's so loud.</i>

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.980
Just hearing that pisses me off!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.980
How about if I give
that woman a talking-to?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.190
I'll tell her what time it is!

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:40.990
But...

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.200
that's fine as it is.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:47.240
She doesn't want him
to take responsibility or anything.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.740
Then, what's to be angry about?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.160
What's to be... angry about?

00:12:53.160 --> 00:13:00.000
If he didn't lay a finger on you and you
don't want him to take responsibility...

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:03.510
then, what's to be angry about,
Miss Shinomiya?

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.760
I can't say.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.310
<i>I just can't say it!</i>

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.270
<i>That I actually wanted him
to do something, just a little!</i>

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.640
I'm sorry.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.980
<i>Am I really that unappealing?</i>

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.980
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.770
<i>I can't tell her I'm angry
about something that silly!</i>

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.030
<i>Of course I can't tell anyone about that!</i>

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.280
That? Th-Th-That?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:29.330
That's how a guy should be like when
a woman is pissed about some trivial thing.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.410
Anyway, for a man to try to understand
everything about a woman,

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.540
it's probably just a fool's errand.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:39.880
In the end, your friend
should just chill out until the heat's off.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.550
If he doesn't have anything
to feel guilty about,

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.050
then there's no need for him to apologize.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.260
Nothing to feel guilty about, huh?

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:10.320
Shinomiya, there's something
I have to tell you.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.330
What is it?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:17.750
I told you I didn't lay a finger on you,

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.080
but...

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.710
the truth is...

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.670
I did lay just one finger on you!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.260
Where did you...

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.220
touch me?

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:36.980
Your lips.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.730
I maybe just tapped them
with my pointer finger.

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:46.780
I mean, not in any weird sense
or like a prank or—

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:47.950
President...

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.240
Now we're even.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:09.380
Starting tomorrow,
we'll be back to normal, right?

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.760
Y-Yeah.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.280
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.910
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.280
<i>They both won.</i>

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.910
THEY BOTH WON
(SUCCESSFULLY MADE UP)

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.910
PASSING BY

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:35.910
HUH...

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.410
Great work, student council!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:43.170
And it's summer vacation
starting tomorrow!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.420
- Yay!
- Yay!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.420
RUSTLE RUSTLE

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.920
Do you have any special plans,
Shinomiya?

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.680
Go shopping a little is about all.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.930
Will you be busy working, President?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.100
Nope.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.640
MIYUKI SHIROGANE
WANTS TO GO SOMEWHERE

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.980
When they adjusted the schedule,
they kind of short-sheeted me.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.060
That leaves me
with a lot of time on my hands.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.310
I'd like to do something.

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:06.570
Yes, I'd like to do something.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.150
- Right, Fujiwara?
- Right, Miss Fujiwara?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.200
SUMMER VACATION PLANS!!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.200
<i>Summer vacation plans!</i>

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.200
<i>- Mountains!
- Beach!</i>

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.910
<i>Mt. Osore!</i>

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:19.580
<i>The topic of a trip was discussed once
but ended up getting put off.</i>

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.960
<i>Will it come to nothing or be carried out?</i>

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.710
<i>The moment had come
to make that decision.</i>

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.550
<i>There are many events that take place
during summer vacation.</i>

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:30.760
AUGUST

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:33.970
TRIP
FIREWORKS
SUMMER FESTIVAL
BBQ
BEACH

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.800
<i>Whether a coed group
goes to these events together</i>

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.970
<i>all depends on whether
they get off to a good start.</i>

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.430
<i>By going somewhere together
for the first time...</i>

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.180
<i>"Where should we go next?"
"Let's all go somewhere again."</i>

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:40.980
<i>And that opens up possibilities.</i>

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.850
<i>On the other hand,
if they stumble at the start,</i>

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.480
<i>the psychological hurdle
for a coed plan becomes higher!</i>

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.070
<i>Boys will stick with the boys,
girls with the girls,</i>

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.990
<i>and that's how they'll spend
summer vacation.</i>

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.780
<i>If they fail here,
it'll be a gray summer vacation!</i>

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.990
THE GIRL'S SANDAL BREAKS,
AND I MUST CARRY HER

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:03.080
<i>No! No! No! No! No! No!
No! No! No! No! No! No!</i>

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.990
TEST OF COURAGE

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:02.040
GOING HOME
TO THE COUNTRY
AND SEEING YOUR
CHILDHOOD FRIEND

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:02.040
TIME LEAPS AND
DIFFERENT DIMENSION
SUMMONS

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:02.580
ONE-SUMMER
ADVENTURES
ARE SURELY
NOT POSSIBLE

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.410
DOING
HOMEWORK
TOGETHER

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.750
LOVEY-DOVEY
WORDS THAT GET
MUTED THROUGH
EXPLODING
FIREWORKS

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.750
GOING ON
COED TRIPS
TOGETHER

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.750
OH NO,
I NEED
TO DO CPR

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.750
FINDING LOVE
AT THE TEMP JOB

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:03.750
<i>Nooo!</i>

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:03.750
SWIMSUITS AND BBQ
AT THE BEACH

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.500
<i>Reality!</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.880
<i>That's what reality is!</i>

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.340
<i>A trip with Shinomiya?</i>

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.800
<i>Of course I wanna go!</i>

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:17.390
<i>But if I bring up the idea of a trip here...</i>

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:22.390
<i>Oh, President...
Are you bringing up that again?</i>

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:27.270
<i>That was like a one-shot topic. I mean,
it wasn't a serious conversation, right?</i>

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.480
<i>Are you really thinking of going?</i>

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.490
<i>Did you have your heart set on that?</i>

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.240
<i>How cute.</i>

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.990
AAAH

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:37.990
<i>That would happen!</i>

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:41.120
Summer! Summer! Summer vacation!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:42.120
<i>You're the one who brought up a trip!
What are you doing just dancing around?</i>

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.790
Summer vacation! Summer vacation!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.120
Fujiwara!

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.870
Summer is the time...

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.420
when you wanna just go all out
and spread your wings, right?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.840
DI... VERSION

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:53.960
Right! Summer is the time you wanna
do something you usually can't do!

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.470
Like a trip would be great!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.720
<i>Yeah, that's it!</i>

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.550
A trip, huh?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:01.850
Sure, everyone needs time away from
the hustle and bustle of life in the city, right?

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:02.600
Yes!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:06.600
I'm going to Hawaii for about a week!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.600
<i>This is gonna work!</i>

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.230
<i>You can go to hell!</i>

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.860
<i>You're the one who said before
you wanted to go on a trip with everyone!</i>

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.780
<i>What's the idea of taking the lead
and acting like you're Hawaiian?</i>

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.780
<i>Aloha in Honolulu!</i>

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.490
<i>Shinomiya, she's your whatever,
isn't she? Do something!</i>

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:21.950
Yes.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.540
A trip... is a good idea.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.540
<i>Kaguya also understands the importance</i>

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.000
<i>of getting off to a good start
for summer vacation.</i>

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:31.920
<i>However, she's known Fujiwara
for a long time</i>

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.260
<i>and thus realizes there is no chance
that Fujiwara will behave to one's satisfaction.</i>

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:40.510
<i>Therefore, there is nothingness!
The empty mind that has checked out!</i>

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.760
<i>Breathing is fun.</i>

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:46.520
NOTHING...

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:46.520
<i>It's no use! I don't sense
any drive in Shinomiya!</i>

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:50.650
<i>W-Well, if Fujiwara is going on a trip,
that's all she wrote.</i>

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.280
<i>The idea of all of us going somewhere
on a trip was a tall order to begin with.</i>

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.440
<i>But at least...</i>

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.160
<i>At least go somewhere
on a day trip and have fun!</i>

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.530
<i>But...</i>

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.370
<i>Go somewhere without Miss Fujiwara?</i>

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:08.080
<i>In other words, you want to go somewhere
with me and not with Miss Fujiwara?</i>

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.920
<i>Oh my.</i>

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.540
<i>How cute.</i>

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.420
<i>I'm checkmated!</i>

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.420
AAAH

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.800
<i>Without Fujiwara,
it won't get off the ground!</i>

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.800
<i>Aloha! Honolulu!</i>

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.800
<i>Can she do something like a week
after she gets back from her trip?</i>

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:22.800
Fujiwara...

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:25.930
A trip abroad is fine,
but so is a trip here, right?

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.770
There are a lot of events during summer.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.520
What are you talking about?

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:36.820
SERIOUS SERIOUS

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.190
Second-year summer is crunch time
for university entrance exams!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.610
I don't have time
to fritter away on having fun!

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.820
<i>You asshole!</i>

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.530
You'd say that when you're the one
who's going on a trip?

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:43.160
Exactly! I'm keeping a balance
between work and play!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.660
<i>Dammit! That's a fair argument!</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.700
<i>President, don't bother.</i>

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.540
<i>You'll never be able to control Fujiwara.</i>

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.920
<i>At a time like this, I think about yummy food.</i>

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:59.670
<i>Crap! I planned to win
Shinomiya's heart this summer!</i>

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:03.970
<i>How cute.</i>

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.560
<i>Whatever pattern I attack,
that's how it ends up!</i>

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.350
<i>Is it a lost cause?</i>

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:12.060
But I'd like to do something
to make memories, even just once.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:12.900
<i>Ishigami?</i>

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:16.150
I'm a first-year,
and you're a second-year, President.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.650
Maybe next year, with studying
for university entrance exams,

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:24.320
there won't be time for anything.
Maybe this is the only year we could hang out.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:25.660
<i>Ishigami...</i>

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.540
<i>This is what you've been thinking?</i>

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:33.960
<i>That's right. Summer isn't
just about hanging out with girls.</i>

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.800
<i>Having dumb fun with guy friends...
That's summer, too.</i>

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.130
Let's go, Ishigami.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.760
There's a big festival
at the end of summer.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.300
I can treat you to takoyaki.

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.300
Summer festival?

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.010
Let's go! Let's go!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.810
<i>What happened to crunch time?</i>

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.560
That's a great idea!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.060
Cotton candy! The shooting game!

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.100
Fireworks!

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:55.440
<i>Fireworks?</i>

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.980
<i>Fireworks with the president?</i>

00:20:58.820 --> 00:20:59.820
<i>I'm in!</i>

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.780
The festival is on August 24th, right?

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.570
I'll keep my schedule open.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.740
Yes, me, too.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:12.580
Wait. I can't make it. I'll be
in Spain then for the tomato festival.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.290
<i>Go to the festival in hell, idiot!</i>

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.830
<i>How many trips are you taking?</i>

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.840
<i>Oh no! Worldly desires! Worldly desires!</i>

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.840
<i>Her empty mind collapsed.</i>

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.130
Don't tell me you're gonna go!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:23.840
Well...

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:29.850
You guys would be so mean to go
to a summer festival without me?

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.930
Yeah, why not?

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:36.270
You're going to the tomato festival,
aren't you, Fujiwara-senpai?

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:39.860
You're gonna have fun there,
but telling us not to go? Give me a break.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:46.610
WAAAAH

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.610
You're so mean to me, Ishigami!

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.990
Idiot! Cold-blooded human!
Your bangs are too long!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:56.620
Ishigami, I hope you burn
your tongue on a takoyaki!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:59.630
I did it again.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.130
I'm going home.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:08.050
Wait, Ishigami.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:09.850
You were in the right today.

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:12.010
<i>Results of today's match...</i>

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:15.140
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:14.520
<i>Victory for everyone except for Fujiwara.</i>

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:15.140
VICTORY FOR EVERYONE EXCEPT FOR FUJIWARA
(FOR SUCCESSFULLY MAKING A PLAN
TO GO TO THE SUMMER FESTIVAL)

00:22:15.390 --> 00:22:18.230
Well, let's meet there on that day at 7 pm.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:19.940
Yes, I'm looking forward to it.

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:24.400
<i>And so, we embark on a new chapter!
Men and women's summer vacation!</i>

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:29.910
OH NO

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:29.910
PADDED

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:29.910
I SEE...
